    "model_design": "Increase weight_decay from 0.05 to 0.1 in AdamW for both models. Add a dropout of 0.2 to the classifier head (currently default 0.1 in RoBERTa) by modifying model.classifier's dropout layer: model.classifier.dropout = nn.Dropout(0.2). Remove discriminative learning rates and layer grouping functions (get_layer_groups, create_optimizer_with_discriminative_lr). Use a single AdamW with lr=2e-5 and weight_decay=0.1 for all parameters. Keep label smoothing at 0.1. This strengthens regularization to combat overfitting.",
    "training_evaluation": "Replace the current training function with a simpler single-phase full fine-tuning from epoch 1: remove gradual unfreezing (set_requires_grad calls) and SWA logic. Use a cosine annealing scheduler with warm restarts (torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts, T_0=3, T_mult=2) instead of get_linear_schedule_with_warmup. Train for 15 epochs with early stopping patience=3 based on validation loss, saving the best checkpoint. Do not recreate optimizer inside the loop. Use a fixed optimizer and scheduler created once. This prevents overfitting by avoiding the delayed unfreezing and SWA averaging over bad checkpoints, as supported by historical experiments where simpler full fine-tuning with cosine schedule performed better."
